1
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:04,440
THIS SHOW IS CREATED
FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY

2
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:06,440
THE CHARACTERS, BEHAVIORS
AND EVENTS ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:09,040
THEY ARE NOT INTENDED TO
DEFAME OR CAUSE DAMAGE

4
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:11,440
TO ANY ORGANIZATION OR INDIVIDUAL.
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

5
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,400
-Move it!
-Keep walking!

6
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:25,680
Move!

7
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:28,800
The bloodhounds are moving the targets
through the red zone.

8
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,760
Ready to engage. Awaiting orders.

9
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:36,640
-Hey!
-Where do you think you're going?

10
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:37,920
-Huh?
-Don't hurt her.

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,280
-Sit down!
-Don't try anything.

12
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:40,640
-Hold her down!
-Help!

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,120
You want to try me, you hag?

14
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:48,200
Do you copy? Ready to engage.

15
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,080
-Hey! Don't!
-No!

16
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:53,840
-No!
-Don't shoot!

17
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,640
Requesting authorization.

18
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,040
-Don't!
-Don't shoot her.

19
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,120
-No!
-Please don't.

20
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:02,520
-Don't shoot!
-Let me go.

21
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,440
-Don't shoot!
-Please…

22
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:07,520
Requesting authorization.

23
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,920
BORDER AREA
NO ENTRY WITHOUT PERMISSION

24
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:19,360
-Mom!
-Grandma!

25
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:20,440
Who's next?

26
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,280
Gun, move!

27
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,600
-Go, go.
-Move!

28
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:26,840
Now!

29
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,400
What will you tell his family?

30
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,200
How do you explain his death?

31
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,720
It's over. Go get some rest.

32
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,680
It's over for you bastards,

33
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:01,920
but my friend hasn't even been cremated.

34
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:05,520
What really happened…

35
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,600
that day?

36
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:13,200
The unit issued a statement.
There was a clash at the border.

37
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:15,200
Your friend died in the line of duty.

38
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,600
In the line of duty

39
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:19,000
or following secret orders?

40
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,400
We'll take the best possible care
of his family.

41
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:24,160
Dumping an orphan in state care?
Is that taking care of them?

42
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,320
-That's enough, Gun.
-When someone dies,

43
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,080
you drape a flag over the coffin,

44
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:32,960
throw some money at the family,
and pretend everything is clean.

45
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,480
We're just guard dogs
at the border to you.

46
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:42,280
-Easily replaced when we die.
-Watch your mouth.

47
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:45,320
I lay in that hospital bed for days,
and then I realized something.

48
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:48,240
That day,

49
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,040
you didn't push in, not because
you couldn't save anyone,

50
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,440
but because that land

51
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:58,720
was still making money for you bastards.

52
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:03,480
You talk like that,

53
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,120
and I could have you discharged right now.

54
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:07,920
I became a soldier

55
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:10,560
to save lives.

56
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
But if I have to serve corrupt scoundrels,

57
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:16,320
I'm done here.

58
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:20,320
From today on…

59
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:24,760
we're no longer commander and soldier.

60
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,480
Just two equal men.

61
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,520
And if anyone else dies…

62
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,640
I'll make you pay.

63
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:30,200
‎GREAT JAPANESE FOOD AT FAIR PRICES
‎SASHIMI SET STARTING AT 280 THB

64
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:48,960
What's the status?

65
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:55,280
Target has arrived, Inspector.

66
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:18,840
Mr. James, Boss is waiting over there.

67
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:22,520
I never use my real name for business.

68
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:24,920
Who the hell are you?

69
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:31,480
-Hey!
-Stay back!

70
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:36,320
-Damn it.
-Hey, follow them!

71
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:40,120
‎Hey!

72
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:44,560
-This way. Come on.
-Go!

73
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:56,520
Secure them. And you, follow me.

74
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,040
Stay down!

75
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:02,280
Follow them!

76
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,680
-Ugh.
-Stop right there!

77
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,720
Hey!

78
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:26,960
-Hold it! Freeze!
-Whoa.

79
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:28,200
Okay, I surrender.

80
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:51,680
Aut, arrest him.

81
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:53,720
Yes, sir.

82
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:10,760
Huh?

83
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,800
Boss.

84
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:53,000
The hitmen we sent failed,

85
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,760
and the police wiped them all out.

86
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:58,320
As for Gun, he didn't follow your orders.

87
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:01,240
What did he do?

88
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:03,840
He killed the target's son.

89
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:07,960
That bastard's something else.

90
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,680
Kill the father, and it ends.

91
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,800
But killing his son?

92
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:19,200
That leaves the father dead inside
for the rest of his life.

93
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:23,200
He wanted him to suffer.

94
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,160
That's exactly why I hired him.

95
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,520
Ordinary hitmen

96
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,880
know how to kill a person.

97
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,520
But this guy…

98
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:41,440
He kills the soul.

99
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,000
Thank you.

100
00:11:57,840 --> 00:11:59,280
Ma'am,

101
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:03,080
I got your medication.
Make sure you take it on time, okay?

102
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:06,720
Thank you, dear.
My memory isn't what it used to be.

103
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:10,720
Why don't you come stay at my house, Rada?

104
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:13,240
Let's see. Look.

105
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,840
Here's my grandson.
Quite handsome, isn't he?

106
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:17,200
Hm?

107
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,760
Is this the one who used to pick you up?

108
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:24,480
I haven't seen him in a while.

109
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:27,240
Oh, he's working on an orchard
in Prachinburi right now.

110
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:29,840
He said he'd be back in a few days.

111
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:33,480
I'll introduce you to him!

112
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:37,360
Sure thing, Grandma.

113
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:46,360
Definitely not an amateur.

114
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,520
One shot, two dead.

115
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:51,280
Why do you think he killed James?

116
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,920
James probably wasn't the main target.

117
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,800
He's flushing someone big out.

118
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,040
Did you get the warrant?

119
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:04,960
Done, sir. We're just waiting
for court approval.

120
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,240
If we catch him,

121
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,400
we find the sniper.

122
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,640
His name is Tongyang.

123
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:38,440
Casinos, gambling dens, brothels,

124
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:40,960
karaoke joints, clubs, bars…

125
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:43,240
The bastard devours everything
in his path.

126
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,520
And he took a bite out of your turf too?

127
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:50,120
In this business, the fastest survives.

128
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:53,000
<i>But he crossed the line.</i>

129
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:08,240
He moved his scammer network
right inside Thailand.

130
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,680
You know, money from these scammers

131
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:15,560
is eating our country up from the inside.

132
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:22,880
<i>So you want to put a stop to him?</i>

133
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:26,160
I'm no saint.

134
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,400
But I can't just stand by

135
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,640
and watch foreigners

136
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:36,080
build an empire
on the blood of our own people.

137
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,240
Just like you.

138
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:43,280
Otherwise, you wouldn't have
walked away from military service.

139
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:10,040
<i>I didn't hire you</i>
<i>because you're a good shot.</i>

140
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,680
I hired you because
you're still full of rage.

141
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,240
Remember that.

142
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:21,040
Is everything clear over there?

143
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:23,040
All clear.

144
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:30,640
Boss, let's get out of here.

145
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,840
Something feels off.

146
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:15,440
Good day.
I'm Police Inspector Sarawut Vorapan

147
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:18,320
from the Cyber Crime Investigation Bureau.

148
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,440
Is there a problem, Officer?

149
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:25,880
I'm here today on official business.

150
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:53,600
Mr. Tongyang, this
is a warrant for your arrest,

151
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,080
regarding scamming charges.

152
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:12,480
Take cover!

153
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:22,319
Aut, secure the area
and call for emergency units!

154
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:23,280
Yes, sir.

155
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:31,640
Guys, there's a sniper in the warehouse.

156
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:34,280
-Everyone, follow me!
-Follow me.

157
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:37,840
Move!

158
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,120
Freeze!

159
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,560
Hey, follow me this way!

160
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:30,800
-Go, go!
-Move!

161
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:53,680
Freeze.

162
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:37,840
Hey, what are you doing?
Get out right now!

163
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:41,200
-Drive.
-Get out.

164
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:06,720
Stop here.

165
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:18,400
Look.

166
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:20,520
Here's my grandson.
Quite handsome, isn't he?

167
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:26,280
You're Grandma Lek's grandson?

168
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:34,120
I have no grandmother.

169
00:21:35,760 --> 00:21:38,200
I'm the nurse who takes care of her.

170
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:41,920
She just showed me your photo today.

171
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:44,800
She was going on
about how handsome you are.

172
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,800
You must keep this a secret.

173
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:51,920
Don't tell anyone. Especially Grandma Lek.

174
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:57,120
People make mistakes. I just want you to--

175
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:59,520
You wouldn't want
to hurt your patient, right?

176
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:06,240
You must lie

177
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:08,960
to help us.

178
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,560
Hey, where are you going?

179
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:10,920
This isn't the amount we agreed on.

180
00:23:19,560 --> 00:23:21,240
You haven't finished the job.

181
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:24,120
Meaning Tongyang is still alive?

182
00:23:25,360 --> 00:23:26,480
Not that.

183
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:30,800
It's because you screwed up.
Someone saw your face.

184
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:34,080
The person who saw your face
is going to drag you down,

185
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:36,080
and I'll go down with you.

186
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:38,040
That woman who saw you…

187
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:41,000
She'll become a witness.

188
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:43,960
You're lucky the police
don't know who you are yet.

189
00:23:45,760 --> 00:23:47,320
You want to close this deal?

190
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:50,200
Go shut her mouth.

191
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:53,280
I don't kill ordinary people.

192
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:58,240
Are you serious right now?

193
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:01,360
Since when did you stop
killing ordinary people?

194
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:05,480
You already killed James.

195
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:08,360
He was ordinary to someone too.

196
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:09,600
She has no part in this.

197
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:11,880
Dead people don't talk.

198
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:13,360
Come on. Be careful.

199
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:16,240
The cops will reach your grandma
before you do.

200
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:17,560
Leave my grandmother

201
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:20,080
out of this.

202
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:23,800
Fine. Then go silence her.

203
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:52,400
Is a guy like him actually going to do it?

204
00:24:57,240 --> 00:25:00,480
Right now, he may still think
he has a choice.

205
00:25:00,560 --> 00:25:04,400
He dared to disobey orders today.
Tomorrow he'll betray us, sir.

206
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:06,320
Should I eliminate him now?

207
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,280
If he were going to betray us,

208
00:25:08,360 --> 00:25:10,360
he wouldn't show up for the money.

209
00:25:10,440 --> 00:25:12,280
And you think he'll follow orders?

210
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:14,400
Do you know why I like him?

211
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:20,320
Because he's vulnerable.

212
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:25,240
Which means he still
has something to lose.

213
00:25:26,920 --> 00:25:29,840
People like that are easy to control.

214
00:25:29,920 --> 00:25:33,720
What if he doesn't kill her, Boss?

215
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:39,400
I'll kill the person he loves instead.

216
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:48,360
Hello.

217
00:25:48,440 --> 00:25:49,800
Oh, hello.

218
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:52,000
-Are you all done seeing the doctor?
-Yes, all set.

219
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:53,800
Okay, remember to take your meds.

220
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:56,440
-Will do. See you later.
-Alright.

221
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:57,640
Goodbye.

222
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,040
How are you doing?

223
00:26:02,120 --> 00:26:04,480
-Exhausted?
-We'll be done soon.

224
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:08,040
-I just put a file over here…
-Here.

225
00:26:08,120 --> 00:26:10,600
Oh, okay. Thank you.

226
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:13,880
Okay.

227
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:16,960
Hm, when is the next appointment?

228
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:34,840
-You.
-Come with me.

229
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:37,600
I never said anything to the police.

230
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:39,280
Even for the sketch, I made stuff up.

231
00:26:39,360 --> 00:26:40,720
I said come with me.

232
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:43,320
-Please, just leave me alone.
-Hey, hey!

233
00:26:44,560 --> 00:26:46,360
-Gun!
-Hey. Hey!

234
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:47,320
Stop!

235
00:26:48,600 --> 00:26:49,800
Gun!

236
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:58,080
Hey, let go.

237
00:26:58,160 --> 00:27:00,720
-Who are those people?
-No time to explain. We need to go.

238
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:03,040
Gun, stop right there!

239
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:08,560
Gun! Gun, stop!

240
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:09,560
Gun!

241
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:14,720
Hand the woman over.

242
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,800
Hey. Please help me.

243
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:32,120
Hey…

244
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:38,040
You want her? Take her.

245
00:27:57,560 --> 00:27:58,480
Come on.

246
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:02,960
You bastard!

247
00:29:14,480 --> 00:29:17,480
Who on earth are those people?
Why are they trying to kill me?

248
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:19,920
Calm down.

249
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:23,240
I can't tell you much right now,

250
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:27,640
but you need to run.
Go as far away from here as you can.

251
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:30,800
What about my job? My life?

252
00:29:31,840 --> 00:29:33,360
I didn't want it to be like this.

253
00:29:34,840 --> 00:29:36,040
Sorry for dragging you in.

254
00:29:36,960 --> 00:29:38,440
Who are you, really?

255
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:03,000
Grandma. I'm on my way
to pick you up. Pack your things.

256
00:30:03,080 --> 00:30:05,280
I'm sending you a location.

257
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:07,040
Who the hell are you?

258
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:09,480
Grandma! Hello, Grandma!

259
00:30:26,080 --> 00:30:27,360
Run, dear!

260
00:30:28,240 --> 00:30:30,040
-Run!
-Grandma!

261
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:41,120
Attack!

262
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:43,320
Get him!

263
00:30:57,480 --> 00:30:58,840
Should I take him out now?

264
00:31:00,400 --> 00:31:04,080
Boss didn't order that.
He wants him to watch her die.

265
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:21,240
Grandma!

266
00:31:34,560 --> 00:31:35,560
Grandma…

267
00:32:20,320 --> 00:32:22,200
Grandma…

268
00:32:30,040 --> 00:32:31,280
Grandma. Grandma…

269
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:34,160
I…

270
00:32:35,600 --> 00:32:40,680
I… love you…

271
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:10,880
Grandma!

272
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:56,600
Hello.

273
00:34:57,200 --> 00:34:58,960
-Where are you?
-Queue number 35,

274
00:34:59,040 --> 00:35:01,560
please proceed to room number seven.

275
00:35:01,640 --> 00:35:03,120
Why are you still at the hospital?

276
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:06,160
I have patients to care for.

277
00:35:06,240 --> 00:35:08,320
I thought those men
wouldn't come back for me.

278
00:35:08,400 --> 00:35:09,600
I'm coming to get you now.

279
00:35:44,240 --> 00:35:45,760
Our men located him, Boss.

280
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:47,960
He brought the woman with him.

281
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:52,280
I really want to see

282
00:35:53,520 --> 00:35:56,560
how much a guy like him
is willing to sacrifice for this woman.

283
00:35:59,360 --> 00:36:00,520
Maybe

284
00:36:01,240 --> 00:36:03,520
she's more important to him
than we thought.

285
00:36:05,080 --> 00:36:06,320
What do you mean by that?

286
00:36:09,720 --> 00:36:12,960
A guy like Gun
wouldn't take a risk like this

287
00:36:13,600 --> 00:36:14,680
unless he felt something.

288
00:36:17,200 --> 00:36:20,520
Good. I like guys like that.

289
00:36:23,320 --> 00:36:25,040
A man with a heart

290
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:28,160
is much easier to kill
than a man without one.

291
00:36:44,680 --> 00:36:48,280
Hey. That's the guy
who shot at me at the hospital.

292
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:50,200
I know.

293
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:53,640
How did he find us here?

294
00:36:56,280 --> 00:36:58,920
Stay in the car. Don't go anywhere.

295
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:01,000
Trust me.

296
00:37:16,160 --> 00:37:17,520
You shouldn't have helped her.

297
00:37:19,120 --> 00:37:20,080
She's not involved.

298
00:37:20,680 --> 00:37:21,960
Orders are orders.

299
00:37:24,560 --> 00:37:26,000
Then try me.

300
00:38:15,760 --> 00:38:16,600
Hey!

301
00:39:55,400 --> 00:39:58,000
The intel leads straight to the sniper.

302
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:06,640
<i>They broke the law.</i>
<i>So use the law to deal with them!</i>

303
00:40:06,720 --> 00:40:08,240
And how can you be sure

304
00:40:08,320 --> 00:40:09,560
the law still holds power?

305
00:40:09,640 --> 00:40:11,560
How much longer do we have to hide?

306
00:40:11,640 --> 00:40:13,240
Until they can't find you.

307
00:40:13,320 --> 00:40:14,360
What if they do find me?

308
00:40:14,440 --> 00:40:16,240
Then they'll have to get through me first.

309
00:40:16,320 --> 00:40:19,200
<i>I won't cause trouble for any of you.</i>

310
00:40:20,120 --> 00:40:21,640
Kill Gun for me.

311
00:40:23,360 --> 00:40:24,320
Come here.

312
00:40:24,400 --> 00:40:25,880
Right here.

313
00:40:26,960 --> 00:40:28,360
-Aim here.
-Keep standing.

314
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:30,440
Let's go!

315
00:40:30,520 --> 00:40:33,280
Boom! Perfect.

316
00:40:33,360 --> 00:40:34,640
Action!

317
00:40:39,120 --> 00:40:40,480
Go!

318
00:40:40,560 --> 00:40:43,840
-You okay?
-Not sore? Okay!

319
00:40:43,920 --> 00:40:45,880
-Round of applause!
-Clap!

320
00:40:45,960 --> 00:40:47,040
He's not sore.

321
00:40:47,120 --> 00:40:47,960
-Not sore?
-Just hurts.

322
00:40:48,040 --> 00:40:49,720
-Really?
-No, no.

323
00:40:49,800 --> 00:40:51,040
-Just a joke.
-Okay.

324
00:40:51,120 --> 00:40:53,320
-You okay?
-How do we set this up?

325
00:41:25,840 --> 00:41:27,840
Subtitle translation by: Anan Pratchayakul
